.TH SCENE 5
.SH NAME
scene \- meshes and pictures to show
.SH DESCRIPTION
A scene file for
.IR view (1)
has one item per line; # begins a comment, and file names are relative
to the scene file.
.PP
.RS
.nf
mesh NAME FILE.obj [colour R G B] [move X Y Z] [turn X Y Z DEG]...
image NAME FILE.ppm X0 Y0 Z0 X1 Y1 Z1 X2 Y2 Z2
view iso|front|back|left|right|top|bottom
background R G B
.fi
.RE
.PP
The parts of an OBJ file with several objects are named
.IB name / part .
A colour (values 0 to 1) replaces that of the file.
Moves, and turns about the axis X Y Z through the origin, are applied
in order.
A picture (PPM P6, or PAM P7 of RGB or RGB_ALPHA) fills the
parallelogram of its corners X0 (lower left), X1 (lower right) and X2
(upper left).
Pictures are blended over the meshes by their opacity, farthest first;
transparent pixels cannot be picked.
The background is grey unless given.
.SH SEE ALSO
view(1), tomesh(1)
